@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+# Create JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`createPatch(from, to)` is exported from `src/index.ts`. It returns a JSON Patch (array of operations) that `applyPatch(from, patch)` turns into `to`. Neither argument is mutated and the patch shares no structure with them. Inputs that are not JSON values throw.
+
+## Minimality
+- Equal values produce `[]`.
+- Objects: members only in `from` are removed, members only in `to` are added, common members are diffed recursively. Unchanged members are never mentioned.
+- Values of different types (or differing scalars) are `replace`d at their path (root path is `""`).
+- Arrays: items are aligned with a longest common subsequence (deep equality). Inserted items are `add`ed, deleted items are `remove`d, surrounding items are untouched. A moved item becomes a `remove` plus an `add`. Where an item was changed in place, it is diffed recursively instead of removed and re-added.
+- Pointer tokens are escaped (`~` -> `~0`, `/` -> `~1`); `__proto__` is an ordinary key.
